The process-wide barrier of the GC on witos (plan step R1.2b): the layer-2 triple defines __linux__, but WitOS has no
Linux UAPI headers; the GC takes musl's <sys/membarrier.h>, as it takes FreeBSD's, and musl's membarrier(cmd, flags),
which has no processor argument. The system layer serves the private expedited barrier with the kernel's process write
barrier.

The size of the processor's cache (plan step P6): musl's sysconf names no cache and WitOS has no /sys, so the GC found
none, and a workstation GC's least generation 0 budget fell to 160 KiB (256 KiB, the floor, by 5/8) where a Linux
without the cache in its sysfs gets 2 MiB on up to four processors. WitOS takes the heuristic upstream gives that Linux
(4 MiB for up to four processors, 8, 16 and 32 MiB beyond).

